<title>FINLAND: Finnair to sell property for FIM 333 mln.</title>
<headline>Finnair to sell property for FIM 333 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national carrier Finnair Oy said in a statement on Monday it would sell its Hotel Inter-Continental property for 333 million markka.</p>
<p>Finnair also said it would sell its 49 percent stake in Hotel Savoy in Moscow.</p>
<p>&quot;The arrangements made will have a positive impact on Finnair's result,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The buyer -- a real estate company to be owned by the state's  Alko-Yhtiot (41 percent), Finnair (40 percent) and engineering group Metra (19 percent) -- would also buy Metra's Hotel strand Inter-Continental, it said.</p>
</text>
